  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-5546",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The computer has $4$ levers, each of which has $3$ positions. Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Total Number of Settings} & =\\text{Number of positions of the }1\\text{st lever} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of positions of the }2\\text{nd lever} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of positions of the }3\\text{rd lever} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of positions of the }4\\text{th lever} \\\\  & =3\\times 3\\times 3\\times 3 \\\\  & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $81$ possible combinations of settings.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
